course: dictionary
lesson: 3739
title: A word that points to a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. Florentine is one of them. It means from or about Florence, a famous city in Italy. Florence is known for art and for the Renaissance, a time when painters and sculptors made some of the world's best-known works.
explain: The same word can point to different things. In «the Florentine Codex», Florentine tells you the book is connected to Florence. A florentine can also be a biscuit, or part of the name of a dish, «eggs florentine». Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: Read the example carefully: «After the conquest, Nahua writers working with the Spanish friar Bernardino de Sahagún recorded Aztec memories of the conquest in the Florentine Codex.» The clues are the Aztec memories and the friar. Florentine is the name of the codex, so you can tell it is a name, not a food.
fact: Florentine means from or about Florence, a city in Italy.
fact: Florence is famous for art and for the Renaissance.
fact: A florentine can be a thin, crisp biscuit made of nuts and candied fruit, often with chocolate on one side.
fact: «Eggs florentine» is a dish served with spinach.
fact: «The Florentine Codex» is a book linked to Florence, written with the help of Nahua writers and the Spanish friar Bernardino de Sahagún.
exercise: What does Florentine mean in «Florentine art»? | A Spanish friar | *From or about Florence, a city in Italy | A thin, crisp biscuit | A breakfast with spinach
exercise: Mum orders «eggs florentine» at the café. What comes with it? | Sausages | Chips | *Spinach | Ice cream
exercise: In «the Florentine Codex», which word tells you the book is linked to a city? | *Florentine | Friar | Codex | Aztec
test: In «a chocolate florentine», what is a florentine? | A painter from Florence | A Spanish friar | *A thin, crisp biscuit with nuts and candied fruit | A breakfast with spinach
test: In history lessons, Florentine painters like Michelangelo and Leonardo were part of which period? | The Stone Age | The Victorian era | The Ice Age | *The Renaissance
exam: In «the Florentine Codex», what does Florentine tell you about the codex? | *It is linked to Florence, a city in Italy | It is a biscuit | It was written by a Spanish friar | It is a breakfast dish
